ThousandShips  Hi. I want to get clarity on the best way to submit once I'm done. Do I submit the python generator script or the actual api files? Or both? The api files have an insane amount of lines added, like 3 to 5 million. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4487849524/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4487920094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119330#issuecomment-4487920094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119330","id":4487920094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC4A53g","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-19T12:53:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T12:53:00Z","body":"If they're generated they shouldn't be included I assume, but I don't know what this does so that's probably something you need to figure out depending on what your PR actually does","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4487920094/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4740728036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119330#issuecomment-4740728036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119330","id":4740728036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGpHE5A","user":{"login":"tommygrammar","id":77222040,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MjIyMDQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77222040?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar","html_url":"https://github.com/tommygrammar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tommygrammar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-18T09:55:36Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T09:55:36Z","body":"> If they're generated they shouldn't be included I assume, but I don't know what this does so that's probably something you need to figure out depending on what your PR actually does\r\n\r\n@AThousandShips  I pushed extension_api.json for this build. Its needed by the generator in this iteration. Still working on a way too incoporate it into the build.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4740728036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5119018483","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119330#issuecomment-5119018483","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119330","id":5119018483,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMR4F8w","user":{"login":"GabCoolDude","id":123309403,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1mNWw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123309403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude","html_url":"https://github.com/GabCoolDude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T14:19:54Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T14:19:54Z","body":"Sorry, but I do not see how this is a valid solution.\r\n\r\nFor starters, the fact that this is a separate module to GodotSharp (aka the mono module) has a lot of problems:\r\n- No Godot data types and classes, as they are all in GodotSharp. To fix this, you rewrote all of the data types manually (**without any interop**) and [added python scripts to generate the classes.](https://github.com/tommygrammar/godot/blob/931eda592924fcb0849497823762a99ff33d4dfd/modules/cross_runtime/gen_cs.py) To state the obvious, this is not a good fix, as there definitely will be differences in behavior between GodotSharp and this module.\r\n- To continue my last point, it actually seems that you decided to write python generators for all classes, not only for C#, but also for C++ and JS. I guess this is what \"Cross runtime Solution\" means, but there are definitely better ways to do this (and they already exist in the form of other PRs)\r\n- The separation is just unnecessary, for this to be usable you'd need both the mono module and this. So why not just put this into the mono module in the first place ?\r\n\r\nThe entirety of `extension_api.json` is included in this PR, which not only blows up the size of this PR to be `+387247`, but is also wrong as `extension_api.json` changes practically daily when new enums, signals, properties, methods and classes get added to Godot. This would be impossible to maintain.\r\n\r\nThere is no editor integration at all. How is the user supposed to run this ? Usually there would be an export plugin alongside some changes to `EditorExportPlatformWeb` so that the export window wouldn't complain when trying to export with C#, but here there is nothing, at all. The only way to get an HTML file with this is to use the `build_all.py` script in the PR, for which you'd need to download the source code.\r\n\r\nThese flaws are pretty obvious, even at glance, which made me wonder how this could ever be submitted, even as a draft. For this to actually be mergeable, you'd essentially need to rewrite everything and start from scratch. To me, it feels like this PR was sloppily thrown together (aka made with AI) with the only goal of getting the bounty.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5119018483/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]